rt session (Context A: Claude Opus 5.5, 09-26\u219209-28; Context B: Claude Sonnet 5.5, resumed 10-01) rebuilt the `llama.cpp-sycl-f16-git` AUR package (Raudbjorn fork) across commits b10146\u2192b12321 on an Arch host (`vinbonesjr`) with a Ryzen 7900X3D and Intel Arc A770 16 GB.\n\n- **Major work areas:** The session covered PKGBUILD rework, a d37dd50bb LLAMA_SUBPROCESS ABI trap, SYCL graphs, the oneAPI 2026.0\u21922026.1 (DLE) swap, oneDNN A/B comparison, a PR #63 benchmark review, a DG2 XMX-gather IGC crash patch, 256-GRF kernels, and an investigation into a 12-vs-18 tokens/s decode discrepancy.\n\n- **Driver switch:** The A770 moved from i915 to the **xe** driver between the two contexts (done by other sessions), and the final build used kernel `7.3.0-rc5-273-linux73-tkg-bore-rc5-xe` with the GPU bound to xe.\n\n- **Key technical finding:** The 12-vs-18 t/s decode issue was traced to a **benchmark methodology error** (a `for` loop reusing a single context with no KV reset), not a real regression\u2014corrected via per-run context creation.\n\n- **Performance results"}